Ladybird’s RequestServer reports how much of a request body curl has
sent, at most every 50ms, and Fetch turns each report into a chunk for
processBodyChunk, so XHR’s upload progress events follow the upload.
The other engines report upload progress from their network processes
the same way. Chromium’s URLLoader sends OnUploadProgress, sampled
every 100ms (kUploadProgressInterval) by its UploadProgressTracker.
WebKit’s NetworkResourceLoader::didSendData() is relayed to the web
process’s WebResourceLoader::didSendData(). And while it’s uploading,
Gecko’s XMLHttpRequestMainThread::OnProgress() takes the bytes sent
from the channel’s progress reports.
